417 true] [17592186444145 1075 #edb/ref 17592186444125 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444145 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444145 1077 "field-3" 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444145 1078 #edb/ref 17592186444120 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444145 1079 #uuid "c7391bdf-0a46-510a-b0ad-0b46b06955a6" 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444146 1075 #edb/ref 17592186444122 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444146 1075 #edb/ref 17592186444129 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444146 1075 #edb/ref 17592186444136 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444146 1075 #edb/ref 17592186444137 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444146 1075 #edb/ref 17592186444139 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444146 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444146 1077 "selection" 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444146 1078 #edb/ref 17592186444139 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444146 1079 #uuid "cfc6238d-540c-5d03-81af-c08e27ebdfce" 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444147 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444143 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444147 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444144 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444147 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444145 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444147 1069 "q-333222" 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444147 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444147 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=5x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=3y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below regarding the given decoupled system of linear differential equations.\n\n$\\,$\nThe $x$-axis is a {{field-1}} line.\n\n$\\,$\nThe $y$-axis is a {{field-2}} line.\n\n$\\,$\nThe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-3}}." 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444147 1072 #uuid "2cc95b14-28b1-5770-bd6e-4ea958da90bb" 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444147 1074 "Writing our system in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nRecall that a homogeneous system of linear differential equations has a single equilibrium (fixed point) at the origin.\n\nSince our system is decoupled, its eigenvectors are the following:\n\n- Eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=5$ with the eigenvector $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ The corresponding straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{5t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $x$-axis and move away from the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, the $x$-axis is the $\\text{unstable}$ line.\n\n- Eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}=3$ with the eigenvector $[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ The corresponding straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{3t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $y$-axis and also move away from the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, the $y$-axis is the $\\text{unstable}$ line.\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{an unstable node (source)}.$ \n\n**Note:** The phase portrait of the system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/66/665ff96d191a9b2dc6dc57f1c3a97743dcb1a26c4118151716bdf430a4c014f3.png)" 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444148 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444142 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444148 1069 "q-332687" 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444148 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444148 1071 "![](images/39/390321da0e4c3367d121a1561ccc41ca4960c912ff53d909acd1c90f505758ce.png)\n\nConsider the phase portrait for a decoupled system above.\nWhich of the following systems could correspond to the given portrait?" 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444148 1072 #uuid "4e106ec5-d244-5095-9a3e-86feed9bed83" 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444148 1074 "Writing a decoupled system in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {\\lambda }_{2}\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince our system is decoupled, its eigenvectors are parallel to the axes. These correspond to so-called straight-line solutions of the form\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,{c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, notice that:\n\n- The tangents along the $x$-axis are pointing away from the origin, meaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$\nmust approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have ${\\lambda }_{1}>0.$\n\n- The tangents along the $y$-axis are pointing toward the origin, meaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nmust approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have ${\\lambda }_{2}<0.$\n\nAmong the options, the only system that satisfies ${\\lambda }_{1}>0$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}<0$ is the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=5x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-2y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444149 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444146 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444149 1069 "q-333183" 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444149 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444149 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=2y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could represent the phase portrait of the decoupled system above?" 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444149 1072 #uuid "97c6c7fa-18db-5e5d-84d1-3076bd6f5c92" 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444149 1074 "Writing our system in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince our system is decoupled, its eigenvectors are the following:\n\n- Eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=1$ with the corresponding eigenvector $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}=2$ with the corresponding eigenvector $[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nThe general solution of the system is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, notice that:\n\n- The straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $x$-axis. Since ${e}^{t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\n- The straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $y$-axis. Since ${e}^{2t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nAmong the given options, there are two phase portraits satisfying these conditions:\n\n![](images/a2/a2c81ff3c50013c149dc6a5db67bbe11cccdbbef22ce2c0712101f4a358bcb8c.png)\n\nLet's consider the solutions $x(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{t}$ and $y(t)={c}_{2}{e}^{2t}$ provided that ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\ne 0.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}=\\frac{({c}_{2}{e}^{2t})^{′}}{({c}_{1}{e}^{t})^{′}}=\\frac{2{c}_{2}{e}^{2t}}{{c}_{1}{e}^{t}}=\\frac{2{c}_{2}}{{c}_{1}}{e}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\to \\pm \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ meaning that the tangents to the solution become more and more vertical as we move away from the origin. This corresponds to the following phase portrait:\n\n![](images/9a/9ab329eed7e67e017a822e8d5163b331e0c93a9747f74aee3a10d6592f44a59b.png)" 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444150 1058 #edb/ref 17592186444151 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444150 1062 #uuid "0f0eb2d5-220a-51b8-8ecc-e34f70d2ec6c" 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444150 1063 #edb/ref 17592186305096 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444151 1058 #edb/ref 17592186444154 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444151 1062 #uuid "54129fc6-c6e7-58f1-988d-b38903f3b41b" 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444151 1063 #edb/ref 17592186391144 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444152 1062 #uuid "aed772c0-58fb-5fcf-9ea0-9de0620f174d" 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444152 1063 #edb/ref 17592186444147 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444153 1058 #edb/ref 17592186444150 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444153 1062 #uuid "c9e90e37-14ef-58a0-a386-45d0aaa27b85" 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444153 1063 #edb/ref 17592186444148 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444154 1058 #edb/ref 17592186444152 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444154 1062 #uuid "dbe1ae80-d585-551e-b83d-d3f42e88a7bb" 13194139534919 17592186045417 true] [17592186444154 1063 #edb/ref 17592186444149 13194139534919 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-9a145625-7556-5712-927a-f0c028bebc85" 17592186444119 "answer-1d7975e3-2735-589b-a5cb-e7baa70e5b2a" 17592186444120 "answer-1e8766a2-b885-5372-9ea9-597fde6b723c" 17592186444121 "answer-24461d44-24c5-575d-be64-3d0e46a32765" 17592186444122 "answer-2af9e8ee-427e-5b4a-9c20-64d8c764d689" 17592186444123 "answer-40549b82-d47f-561c-8931-d7d35ef461cb" 17592186444124 "answer-40931ed8-a2d3-5a7d-af42-4ceeceafa5f1" 17592186444125 "answer-4cfdedb2-5206-5bb7-bc0c-b4380ef84ac3" 17592186444126 "answer-59d44033-2953-53f5-9485-d986fa666d6d" 17592186444127 "answer-6228cec8-4f90-5557-9758-248e08a02159" 17592186444128 "answer-62879d01-d1d9-55e2-ab3d-537c10ca44a9" 17592186444129 "answer-62f8b741-a9bc-5f56-8242-c18d258a8e1e" 17592186444130 "answer-73a7ffd1-1cf0-5378-bc11-62171a0c3abc" 17592186444131